# Force HTTPS: instruct browsers to only ever connect over TLS (mirrors the
# marketing site). The HTTP→HTTPS redirect itself is the Cloudflare zone
# "Always Use HTTPS" setting.
#
# These are served by Workers static assets (wrangler.jsonc — this app is a
# Worker with assets, not a Pages project; `_headers` works the same way for
# both), and the portal Worker passes them through on
# opensource.unisim.co.uk/jukebox/*. `/*` matches every path, prefixed or not.
# The Capacitor and Electron builds load the bundle from disk and never see
# these headers.
#
# Content-Security-Policy (2026-10-12) — what the web app really reaches for,
# and nothing else:
#   • script-src: its own bundle; the one inline script in index.html (the
#     pre-paint theme, allowed by its sha256 — src/lib/csp.test.ts fails the
#     build if the script changes without the hash); Google's sign-in script
#     (the SDK loads accounts.google.com/gsi/client on demand). No
#     'unsafe-inline' and no 'unsafe-eval'.
#   • style-src 'unsafe-inline': React style attributes, everywhere.
#   • connect-src: Supabase (API, auth, storage for a backup to a Universal ID,
#     realtime), the suite changelog, Google sign-in, and the three lookups a
#     user asks for: lrclib.net (lyrics), en.wikipedia.org (About this track),
#     itunes.apple.com plus the chosen picture on *.mzstatic.com (Find a
#     picture, on a request).
#   • worker-src 'self' blob:: the service worker, and Supabase realtime's
#     heartbeat worker (a blob:).
#   • media-src: the music is played from blob: URLs of the user's own files;
#     https: is allowed too so no playback path is refused.
#   • img-src https:: Wikipedia thumbnails, iTunes artwork, avatars.
#   • frame-src: Google sign-in only.
#   • No Cloudflare Web Analytics. Cloudflare's zone-level automatic setup
#     injects its beacon (static.cloudflareinsights.com) into the live HTML;
#     this policy refuses it on purpose. Turn the injection off for this host
#     in Cloudflare (Web Analytics site rules) — until then the beacon is
#     simply refused here.
# The dev server serves the same policy Report-Only (vite.config.ts, cspDev()).
#
# Hardening (2026-10-12). Nothing in the suite frames this app, so refusing to
# be framed elsewhere costs nothing.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-3mZLT8QvXfr7EO+IvEUeiA7ljcfRRFIjG77C5UGG//4=' https://accounts.google.com/gsi/client; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://accounts.google.com/gsi/style; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' data: blob: https://rygfxgalojojppxmhddo.supabase.co wss://rygfxgalojojppxmhddo.supabase.co https://changelog.unisim.co.uk https://accounts.google.com/gsi/ https://lrclib.net https://en.wikipedia.org https://itunes.apple.com https://*.mzstatic.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com/gsi/; media-src 'self' blob: data: https:; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'
